cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Who Gets Funded? An Automated, Explainable Machine-Learning
  Pipeline for Predicting Funding Outcomes and Equity of Access
  in Prosocial Crowdfunding
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Fazal Ur Rehman
    family-names: Cheema
    affiliation: Queen's Business School, Queen's University Belfast
repository-code: 'https://github.com/cheemafazal-lab/who-gets-funded'
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end pipeline for predicting funding outcomes in
  prosocial crowdfunding and auditing the equity of access to
  algorithmic recourse. The outcome is modelled as the fractional
  share of the requested amount raised, using a Papke-Wooldridge
  fractional logit baseline and gradient-boosted trees, with
  TreeSHAP attribution and counterfactual search restricted to
  an explicitly defined actionable feature set. Equity is assessed
  across four distinct dimensions: outcome disparity, prediction
  disparity, error-rate disparity, and the cost of recourse.
keywords:
  - crowdfunding
  - microfinance
  - explainable-machine-learning
  - algorithmic-recourse
  - counterfactual-explanations
  - fairness-auditing
  - fractional-response-models
  - gradient-boosting
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-09-11'
